== Round 30: structure of orbit 28's zero set (h30_zeros.py 28 1000 3; h30_zeros_hess.py 28; ad hoc sampling)
   948/1000 starts reach lambda_min < 1e-11. At 20,000 uniform random points, lambda_min < 1e-9 at a fraction 5e-4 and the median is 3.1e-3 (57/69/75/81: minimum over the sample >= 2.6e-3, median ~0.15).
   lambda_min = 0 IDENTICALLY on the hypersurfaces t0 in {0,pi} and t1 in {0,pi} (20,000 random points each, all < 1e-9; max |value| ~1e-15). Not on t2 = 0 alone (fraction 0.003).
   Zeros found: 45% have sin t0 = 0, 45% sin t1 = 0, none both, 10% neither (e.g. a2 = 0 with sin t2 = 0, or slow convergence near the hypersurfaces).
   Kernel at t0 = 0 lies in the z0 = 0 subspace (z = 0..3); at t0 = pi in span(z = 4, 6); at t1 = 0 in span(0, 1, 4, 5); at t1 = pi in span(3, 7).
   Hessian rank of lambda_min at simple zeros (FD, threshold 1e-3): 0 or 1 -> zero set of codimension 1 (hypersurfaces).
   Spectra of 28 and 30 at random points agree to ~1e-3 (both near {0,0,1/3,1/3,1/3,2/3,2/3,2/3}; trace 3).
   Witness search next to the hypersurfaces (h30_kappa.py, 400 starts, delta = 1e-2 and 1e-3): 28 min lambda/delta^2 >= -1.3e-9 (no crossing); control 30 finds -0.0422 at t0 = delta and t1 = delta (its crossing).
   Facial reduction at KP=0,1 with these 921 zeros (991 kernel vectors): face dimension 41 of 8800 -> the hypersurface zero set leaves almost no room for a certificate in this basis.
   Further zero component: lambda_min = 0 identically on {a2 = 0, sin t2 = 0} (codim 2; 20,000 random points each for t2 = 0 and pi), not on a2 = pi or a0/a1 = 0 with t2 = 0. Same three components for 30. (h30_ratio.py: minimising lambda/(sin^2 t0 sin^2 t1) lands on a2 = 0, sin t2 = 0.)
   At t0 = 0, M + c is block diagonal in z0 (off-diagonal block exactly 0); the z0 = 0 block has spectrum {0, 1/3, x, 2/3 - x} (trace 1), the z0 = 1 block trace 2.
   Weighted terms |xi_k0 xi_k1|^2 sigma (= sin^2 t_k sigma / 4): already contained in the KP basis (monomials xi_k0 xi_k1 * v), so they add nothing new.
   Face problems at gamma = 0 with these zeros (h27_face.py REAL=1 gamma):
     KP=0,1:   face 41 of 8800, equality rows rank 45, dropped rows inconsistent by 1.27 -> PrimalInfeasible
     KP=0,1,2: face 172 of 22000, rank 210, inconsistency 1.42 -> PrimalInfeasible
   So no gamma = 0 certificate exists in these bases (NUMERICAL: depends on the zeros being exact zeros, value < 1e-12): the codim-1 zero set is an obstruction, not a solver-accuracy problem.

